Mods: {
	CalamityLegendsComeBack: {
		Items: {
			Weapons: {
				SeasSearing: {
					DisplayName: Sea-Scorching Heaven - Sea's Searing
					Tooltip: "[GFB]"
					Intro: "[c/58FFDA:Abyssal radiation rifle. Pollution stacks, spreads, and collapses on command.]"

					LeftClick_Phase1: "[c/9AEAFF:Left Click: 3-round burst of pollution rounds (4 frames between shots, 15 frames between bursts). Every main round carries a recon soul that hunts stragglers. The last shot of each burst fires a Pollution Rocket for long-range pursuit.]"
					LeftClick_Phase2: "[c/9AEAFF:Left Click: 4-round burst. Keeps the last-shot Pollution Rocket; the first and last shot each vent one bile spray — front-line pressure with splashes at both ends.]"
					LeftClick_Phase3: "[c/9AEAFF:Left Click: 5-round burst. Keeps the bile sprays and last-shot Rocket; mid-burst rounds scatter a few Pollution Bubbles on hit, forming a brief spreading pollution zone.]"
					LeftClick_Phase4: "[c/9AEAFF:Left Click: 5-round burst. Keeps bile and bubbles; after each completed burst, alternately deploys a heavy companion — Pollution Rocket / twin Skyfin Torpedoes.]"
					LeftClick_Phase5: "[c/9AEAFF:Left Click: 5-round burst. The heavy companion rotation expands to Pollution Rocket / twin Skyfin Torpedoes / Pressure Depth Charge; the last shot of every few bursts triggers a small nuke on hit.]"
					LeftClick_Phase6: "[c/9AEAFF:Left Click: full-auto pollution rounds (one every 4 frames, no burst gap). Every 5 rounds vent a bile spray; every 20 rounds deploy a rotating heavy companion; every 40 rounds instead drop a pair of seeking missiles; every 30th round triggers a small nuke on hit.]"

					RightClick_Tier0: "[c/6FE6B0:Right Click · Pressure Protocol: hold to charge, release for one shotgun volley.]"
					RightClick_Tier1: "[c/6FE6B0:Right Click · Pressure Protocol: a charged release fires one shotgun volley and detonates three abyssal light columns at the cursor.]"
					RightClick_Tier2: "[c/6FE6B0:Right Click · Pressure Protocol: a charged release fires two shotgun volleys and detonates three abyssal light columns at the cursor.]"
					RightClick_Tier3: "[c/6FE6B0:Right Click · Pressure Protocol: a charged release fires two shotgun volleys + three abyssal light columns, and summons a large pollution vortex at the cursor.]"

					EnemyRadiation_Tier0: "[c/B4E24C:Enemy · Radiation Pollution: hits stack pollution, up to grade 2 at this progress. Pollution slows enemies, weakens their defense, boosts your effective armor pen and suppresses life regen; spreads to nearby foes at 12+ stacks; the right-click fission consumes all pollution and detonates by stack count.]"
					EnemyRadiation_Tier1: "[c/B4E24C:Enemy · Radiation Pollution: up to grade 3 at this progress. Slows, breaks defense, spreads and suppresses regen; at grade 3+ a right-click detonation also spawns pollution spikes.]"
					EnemyRadiation_Tier2: "[c/B4E24C:Enemy · Radiation Pollution: up to grade 4 at this progress. Grade 3+ detonations spawn pollution spikes and grade 4+ also spawn a pollution vortex; bosses and worms have higher thresholds and blast scaling.]"
					EnemyRadiation_Tier3: "[c/B4E24C:Enemy · Radiation Pollution: up to grade 5 at this progress (max). At full strength defense effectiveness is cut by up to 42% and effective armor pen rises by up to 8%; grades 1–5 apply -36 / -70 / -130 / -220 / -360 life regen.]"

					PlayerRadiation_Tier0: "[c/FFC94C:Ally · Radiation Excitement: sustained hits build levels (15 / 40 / 80 / 140 cumulative hits unlock levels 1–4), capped at level 1 here — max: +4% ranged damage.]"
					PlayerRadiation_Tier1: "[c/FFC94C:Ally · Radiation Excitement: capped at level 2 here — max: +8% ranged damage, +4 ranged armor pen.]"
					PlayerRadiation_Tier2: "[c/FFC94C:Ally · Radiation Excitement: capped at level 3 here — max: +13% ranged damage, +8 ranged armor pen, +12% move speed.]"
					PlayerRadiation_Tier3: "[c/FFC94C:Ally · Radiation Excitement: capped at level 4 here — max: +19% ranged damage, +13 ranged armor pen, +20% move speed, +10% ranged crit.]"

					Passive: "[c/A0B4C0:Held: emits an abyssal pressure field that slows nearby enemies and slowly seeds pollution.]"
					Ultimate: "[c/FF8A30:Ultimate (Air-to-Ground Nuclear Missile): Press] [[c/FF8A30:{0}]] [c/FF8A30: to charge for one second, then left-click to designate a target for a deep-sea thermonuclear strike. The blast heavily pollutes survivors.]"
					LegendaryHint: "[c/BABABA:Hold Shift to access the disaster record]"
					LegendaryText:
						'''
						[c/58FFDA:The first Sea's Searing only needed to do one thing: put bullets into the target and let pollution begin to spread.]
						[c/4CD268:That design already suited the Sulphurous Sea, but it too easily reduced disaster to damage-over-time numbers.]
						[c/58FFDA:After the rebuild, every shot leaves disaster coordinates, while pollution clouds, cracked light, and acid corrosion stack across the field.]
						[c/4CD268:Right click is no longer just extra damage. It chooses when to detonate the areas already infected.]
						[c/FF8A30:When the final strike lands, what bursts is not one bullet, but the collapse all previous pollution had been pointing toward.]
						'''
				}
			}
		}

